@@NEW
change no record the harness writes (it runs its own parsing under
`LC_ALL=C`, where each byte is one character, so no byte can end a parse, and
a byte >= 0x80 is in no character class, so a record line its ASCII grammar
cannot read is refused by name or, where the harness decides what must be
covered, kept whole; and a parse that fails never reads as a passing result),
while a check whose programs read them pins them or declares
@@END
